        ॰ `मूलांश` of ० as a MISSING PAIR in compiled code while the
        ॰ interpreter keeps `Some(०)` and `शून्यम्` apart — measured, ७००१
        ॰ against ७००२. `मूलांश` is a BIT NUMBER and bit ० is ordinary: 484 of
        ॰ this table's 2801 pairs carry it and EVERY register slot opens with
        ॰ one (`add` carries `0>7`, `0>15`, `0>20`). Those pairs were skipped
        ॰ natively, index ० of `न्यास` was never written, and
        ॰ `सङ्केतनॱअवकाशविस्तारः` — which walks `न्यास` from ० — read
        ॰ `युग्मम् ॱ मूलांश` off a null and faulted at address ०.
        ॰
        ॰ `दशाङ्कवाचकः` asks the question this routine actually means: is the
        ॰ cell a non-empty run of decimal digits. It answers सत्यम् for `0` and
        ॰ असत्यम् for an empty cell or a `-`, which is the same set
        ॰ `दशाङ्कमूल्यम्` refuses — so a MALFORMED pair is still dropped and
        ॰ does not arrive as a present ०. That is the case that must stay
        ॰ REFUSED, and it is what separates this repair from one that writes
        ॰ every pair unconditionally.
        चरः मूलवाचकः ॱॱ बूल भवति सङ्केतन ॱ दशाङ्कवाचकः पाठ्यम् युग्मादिः विरामः ।
