    ॰ SPLIT IN TWO (2026-09-18), because one statement was doing two things and a
    ॰ marker between them is the only way to tell which one faults. The right hand
    ॰ side is a SLICE — `पाठ्यम् अङ्कः X अन्तः Y` builds a FRESH BLOCK — and the
    ॰ left is a field write to a record local declared ०.
    ॰
    ॰ RUNG 86 ALREADY RULES OUT THE FIELD WRITE as the general explanation:
    ॰ `सङ्केतनदोषरचना` (encode.t1:1626) declares `चरः नव ॱॱ सङ्केतनदोष भवति ०` and
    ॰ writes fields to it, and that routine answers ७२४२ NATIVELY. So a ०-declared
    ॰ record local is writable; the slice is what has not been shown.
    चरः आज्ञापाठः ॱॱ अङ्कः अन्तः अ८ भवति पाठ्यम् अङ्कः आज्ञादिः अन्तः आज्ञान्तः ।
