    इति
    ॰ ९६०१ — THE SLICE'S LENGTH, not merely that it returned (2026-09-18).
    ॰ Rung 95 showed `९५०१` reached, so the slice RETURNS. That is not the same as
    ॰ its returning something sound: a run that comes back empty, or with a length
    ॰ the interpreter does not agree on, would return and then be written into a
    ॰ field — and the write is what faults.
    ॰
    ॰ THIS IS THE ALLOCATOR QUESTION IN THE ONLY FORM THE COMPILED SIDE CAN ASK IT.
    ॰ `रचनासूचकः` is an emitter-owned label (ir.t1:587), not a `.t1` variable, so
    ॰ the compiled compiler cannot read its own allocation cursor — a state dump
    ॰ specified in terms of that cursor is not emittable from this side without new
    ॰ runtime support. A run's `दैर्घ्य` IS visible, and a length that differs from
    ॰ the interpreter's is the same evidence one layer up.
    यदि सङ्केतनॱविन्यासमुद्रणार्हम् समम् सत्यम् आदि
